<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ryūzōji Takanobu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1529">1529</a>–<a href="/years/1584">1584</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ryuzoji Takanobu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ryūzōji Takanobu was a Japanese warlord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> from Hizen in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>. A former monk, he overthrew his family's overlords, the Shōni, and became one of the three great powers of Kyushu, known for ruthlessness. He was killed in 1584 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okitanawate">Battle of Okitanawate</a> by the Shimazu and the Arima, and his domain soon passed to his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, the Nabeshima.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ryuzoji-takanobu.jpg" alt="Ryūzōji Takanobu" width="320" height="497" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ry%C5%ABz%C5%8Dji_Takanobu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
